
# Contributing Guidelines
Thank you for your interest in contributing to our project! We welcome suggestions, feedback, and improvements.

## How to Report a Problem
If you find a bug or problem in the project, please open a GitHub Issue. Describe the problem clearly and provide any relevant information to help us understand it.

## How to Suggest Improvements
If you have an idea to improve the project, please open a GitHub Issue to describe your suggestion. The team will review it and discuss possible changes.

## How to Submit Changes
If you would like to contribute code or other changes:

1. Create a new branch for your changes.
2. Make your changes and test them.
3. Commit and push your changes to GitHub.
4. Open a Pull Request (PR) describing your changes.
5. Wait for a team member to review your PR before it is merged.
All Pull Requests must be reviewed and merged by a human team member.

## AI Policy
Contributors may use AI tools to assist with coding, explanations, and debugging.

However:
Contributors should disclose when and how they use AI tools.
AI-generated code and content must be reviewed and tested before submission.
Contributors are responsible for the accuracy and quality of their contributions.
All GitHub Issues and Pull Requests must be created and reviewed by humans. AI tools must not open or merge them on behalf of contributors.

Thank you for helping improve our project!